# forme's copies of skrifa, write-fonts, hayro-write and hayro-syntax

forme builds against its own copy of skrifa 0.42.1 (MIT OR Apache-2.0, https://github.com/googlefonts/fontations), under `vendor/skrifa`, through `[patch.crates-io]`, so that skrifa's hinting code does not link into the WebAssembly module: forme and subsetter draw every outline unhinted, and the TrueType interpreter, the CFF hinter and the autohinter were about a fifth of the module. The copy is the crate as crates.io ships it, with its licence files, and a few lines changed in three files, each of which opens with a line saying so. In `src/outline/mod.rs`, `DrawSettings::unhinted` and `OutlineGlyph::draw` are marked `#[inline(always)]`, so a caller's unhinted settings decide the match at compile time and the hinted arm is dropped; and a constant `HINTING`, false, is added. In `src/outline/glyf/mod.rs` the two places the TrueType interpreter runs, and in `src/outline/cff/mod.rs` the one place the CFF hinter runs, are guarded by `HINTING` as well. And in `src/outline/mod.rs` `OutlineGlyph::draw` hands every pen to the unhinted drawing behind one type, a `DynPen` that forwards the five pen calls through `&mut dyn OutlinePen`, so the glyf scalers and the CFF charstring evaluator are compiled once and not once per pen (forme's bounds pen and subsetter's path pen each had their own copy, about 42 kB of the module). An unhinted draw is unchanged, point for point; a hinted draw in this copy draws unhinted, and nothing in forme asks for one. skrifa has no feature that leaves its hinting out, and subsetter takes it with default features.

forme also builds against its own copy of write-fonts 0.48.1 (MIT OR Apache-2.0, https://github.com/googlefonts/fontations), under `vendor/write-fonts`, through the same `[patch.crates-io]`, so that its table repacker, HarfBuzz's repacker ported with its subtable splitters, does not link. subsetter writes one table through write-fonts, an instanced `glyf` glyph, which has no offsets and which the basic sort always orders. In `src/graph.rs` a constant `PACKING`, false, is added, and `pack_objects` returns false where the basic sort leaves an overflow instead of repacking; the file opens with a line saying so. A table the basic sort orders is written as before. The copy's `Cargo.toml` also allows `dead_code`, since upstream's `TTCHeader` is unused under the features subsetter takes and a path dependency's warnings are not capped. Both copies are the only door: neither crate has a feature that leaves the code out.

forme builds against its own copies of hayro-write 0.7.0 and hayro-syntax 0.7.2 (both MIT OR Apache-2.0, https://github.com/LaurenzV/hayro), under `vendor/hayro-write` and `vendor/hayro-syntax`, through the same `[patch.crates-io]`; hayro-write copies a page of a facsimile's PDF into the file as a Form XObject, and hayro-syntax reads that PDF. Each copy is the crate as crates.io ships it, with its licence files, and every changed file says so in its first line. In hayro-write's `Cargo.toml`, hayro-syntax is asked for `std` alone and not `unsafe`, which would link flate2's inflater beside hayro-syntax's own and memchr.
